{
  "algorithm": "EDDSA",
  "curve": "Ed25519",
  "purpose": "CKM_EDDSA with CK_EDDSA_PARAMS through the PKCS#11 ABI: the three RFC 8032 Ed25519 schemes (pure / ctx / ph) selected by the mechanism parameter, per PKCS#11 v3.2 \u00a76.3.14 Table 73.",
  "_provenance": {
    "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/usnistgov/ACVP-Server/975de31eb83d87039ec88934fdc47d8c312b892d/gen-val/json-files/EDDSA-SigGen-1.0/internalProjection.json",
    "source_release": "975de31eb83d87039ec88934fdc47d8c312b892d",
    "retrieved": "2026-08-29",
    "producer": "NIST ACVP-Server (reference/generator-validated sample vectors)",
    "source_sha256": "794d58fb39f08de4f852d63cb98b95c39bcc38ea42c7d42d09e92c15dadd5d81",
    "note": "vsId 1 AFT groups. tgId 1 = Ed25519 pure (contextLength 0 on all 10 cases); tgId 2 = Ed25519 preHash with a per-case non-empty context; tgId 3 = Ed448 with a per-case non-empty context; tgId 4 = Ed448 preHash with a per-case context. Every selected case was independently re-verified against OpenSSL 3.6.3 through OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_INSTANCE + OSSL_SIGNATURE_PARAM_CONTEXT_STRING before adoption - 40/40 byte-exact. NOTE ON COVERAGE: ACVP EDDSA-SigGen-1.0's sample set contains NO Ed25519ctx case (tgId 1's contexts are all empty, which is pure Ed25519, and every preHash group is Ed25519ph), so Ed25519ctx is carried at Tier 3 from RFC 8032 \u00a77.2 below - the one place on this surface where Tier 1 genuinely does not reach."
  },
  "_provenance_tier3": {
    "source_url": "https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8032.txt",
    "source_release": "RFC 8032 (January 2017), Josefsson & Liusvaara",
    "retrieved": "2026-08-29",
    "producer": "IETF RFC 8032 \u00a77 published test vectors (Tier 3 - used only where NIST ACVP does not publish an equivalent case)",
    "source_sha256": "ed63657ff389301282b169b0abde9b5dd2c7e4d524fdfa5da6ff3094fc93c4c3",
    "note": "Parsed directly from the canonical rfc-editor.org text, not transcribed by hand. All 21 \u00a77.1-\u00a77.5 vectors were re-verified against OpenSSL 3.6.3 through the same instance/context API this engine uses - 21/21 byte-exact. REPLACES, for the Ed448 file, a prior file that declared \"Generated via Node.js crypto (OpenSSL backend), Ed448 (RFC 8032)\": self-generated material, inadmissible as sole evidence under the remediation plan's \u00a71 ladder, and orphaned (loaded by nothing) besides."
  },
